  "issue": {
    "body": "[`request.url_for` takes `Any` for the `path_params`](https://github.com/encode/starlette/blob/217019b36303ea16a5869ad076d835e4fdc1cef3/starlette/requests.py#L168) whereas [`application.url_path_for` expects `path_params` to be `str`](https://github.com/encode/starlette/blob/537ab6afd110b79dca95f3c8ecc6980710b1de1c/starlette/applications.py#L107). Likewise the route / routers expect `path_params` to be `str`. See [here](https://github.com/encode/starlette/blob/537ab6afd110b79dca95f3c8ecc6980710b1de1c/starlette/routing.py#L159) and [here](https://github.com/encode/starlette/blob/537ab6afd110b79dca95f3c8ecc6980710b1de1c/starlette/routing.py#L584).\r\n\r\nThe type mismatch is not caught by the type checker as the `router` here is untyped:\r\nhttps://github.com/encode/starlette/blob/217019b36303ea16a5869ad076d835e4fdc1cef3/starlette/requests.py#L169-L170\r\n\r\nI think `Any` is probably more close to being the correct type as the `path_params` can be `UUID`, `int`, etc.\r\n\r\n[The docs](https://www.starlette.io/routing/#reverse-url-lookups) would make it seems that the API for these two methods should have a consistent signature.",
    "closed_at": "2021-11-30T18:13:09Z",
    "created_at": "2021-10-21T15:26:18Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/1319",
    "labels": [
      "typing"
    ],
    "number": 1319,
    "state": "closed",
    "title": "Inconsistent Typing Between request.url_for and application.url_path_for",
    "user": "cancan101"
  },
